flow path, exactly once. Future version: a future manifest must not silently appear as a new empty conversation without a visible recovery state. Revision ordering: late lower revisions cannot resurrect deleted or older threads. Tombstone ordering: a forged higher revision containing a deleted thread remains rejected. New Conversation during active turn: reset remains blocked while a runtime turn is active. Archived thread: read-only projection, copy, continue-as-new, and delete target the selected thread rather than the hidden active thread. Rethread recovery: a reported successful rethread must correspond to an accepted state transition and actual runtime/thread replacement. Persisted failure: retry safety and recovery actions remain conservative after restart. Mdflow explain failure: raw stderr must stop at diagnostics and not become transcript or user-facing recovery text. Automation projection: active/archive selection, read-only state, lineage, draft presence, and copy eligibility agree with the rendered session. Seeded Flow finding to confirm BUG-FLOW-001 — collision-prone conversation storage key The bundled conversation_file_name sanitizes flow_id and flow_path, truncates the path to 160 characters, and writes no hash of the original path. load_persisted_conversation_from canonicalizes the parsed snapshot to the requested path. A same-ID collision can therefore overwrite or misattribute another project’s transcript. Concrete reproducer: flow_id = "project:review" path A = /work/a-b/flows/review.md path B = /work/a/b-flows/review.md sanitize(A) == sanitize(B) Confirm branch ownership: Bashgit diff -U50 main...HEAD -- src/flows/session.rs | rg -n -C 12 'conversation_file_name|sanitize_component|load_persisted_conversation_from' git show main:src/flows/session.rs 2>/dev/null | rg -n -C 8 'conversation_file_name|sanitize_component' || true Deterministic auxiliary check: Bashpython3 - <<'PY' def sanitize(raw: str) -> str: return "".join(c if c.isascii() and (c.isalnum() or c in "-_") else "-" for c in raw) a = "/work/a-b/flows/review.md".lstrip("/") b = "/work/a/b-flows/review.md".lstrip("/") print(sanitize(a)) print(sanitize(b)) assert sanitize(a) == sanitize(b) PY Label this Verified-Static only when the exact HEAD code and load path are confirmed locally. It becomes a branch regression only if the relevant behavior was introduced or made reachable by this branch. Future remediation pseudodiff, to record but not apply: Diff--- a/src/flows/session.rs +++ b/src/flows/session.rs @@ fn conversation_file_name(flow_id: &str, flow_path: &str) -> String { let id = sanitize_component(flow_id); let mut path = sanitize_component(flow_path.trim_start_matches('/')); const PATH_PORTION_MAX: usize = 160; if path.len() > PATH_PORTION_MAX { path = path[path.len() - PATH_PORTION_MAX..].to_string(); } - format!("{id}--{path}.json") + let identity = crate::ai::reliability::redacted_fingerprint( + &format!("{flow_id}\0{flow_path}") + ); + let identity = sanitize_component(&identity); + format!("{id}--{path}--{identity}.json") } @@ fn load_persisted_conversation_from(...) - let path = dir.join(conversation_file_name(flow_id, flow_path)); + let path = dir.join(conversation_file_name(flow_id, flow_path)); if let Ok(raw) = std::fs::read_to_string(&path) { ... } + // Migration only: inspect the old collision-prone name. + // Adopt it only when its embedded flow_path is empty or exactly matches + // the requested path. Persist the hashed file before removing the old one. Future behavior test: persist A, persist B, load A, load B: A returns only A turns; B returns only B turns; both files coexist; legacy migration refuses a nonmatching embedded flow_path. Mandatory Flow proof-gap probe PersistedAiFailure::to_failure reconstructs every failure with RetrySafety::SameSelectionReadOnly. Determine whether any production restore path calls it: Bashrg -n 'PersistedAiFailure::to_failure|\.to_failure\(\)' src tests No production call: record GAP-FLOW-002, dead or future-facing semantics. Production call: trace original failure safety through persistence and prove that Never or mutation-sensitive failures cannot gain a retry action after restart. Do not claim correctness from the code comment. Batch 3 — Dictation audit Owned files and audit threads src/dictation/types.rs FrozenDictationDestination DictationTargetSelection ImmutableDictationTranscript DictationDeliveryRequest/Outcome DictationMutationReceipt DictationFailureState DictationFailureRecoveryCapabilities ALL_DICTATION_TARGETS DictationSessionPhase::as_automation_str src/dictation/delivery.rs Every target adapter, stale-identity refusal, mutation receipt, duplicate/replay handling, retry-safety classification. src/dictation/history.rs Save-before-safe-claim ordering, atomicity, IDs, retention, lookup and recovery behavior. src/dictation/runtime.rs Capture/finalize/delivery phase transitions, hidden-processing behavior, retry and recovery routing, callback installation. src/dictation/mod.rs State ownership, exports, selection generation, global snapshot helpers. src/dictation/window.rs DictationOverlay resize_overlay_height process_global_keys_if_requested set_state open_dictation_overlay close_dictation_overlay reopen_last_dictation_overlay dictation_native_footer_config automation_layout_info dictation_window_lifecycle_receipt src/dictation/microphone_popup_window.rs build_dictation_microphone_popup_snapshot sync_dictation_microphone_popup_window dismiss_dictation_microphone_popup_from_parent request_close select_row accept_row generation-aware automation cleanup src/dictation/tests.rs Determine which runtime claims are truly exercised versus helper-only tests. Symbol and boundary trace: Bashrg -n \ 'DictationDeliveryRequest|DictationDeliveryOutcome|DictationMutationReceipt|history_saved|safe_message|retry_safety|identity_fingerprint|external_window_id|resize_overlay_height|set_automation_bounds|as_automation_str|format!\("\{:\?\}".*phase|select_row|selected_row_id|upsert_dictation_microphone|dismiss_dictation_microphone_popup_from_parent|dictation_window_lifecycle_receipt' \ src/dictation src/windows tests scripts Required Dictation scenarios External application changes after recording begins: refuse rather than paste into the new app. External window identity changes while the PID remains the same: refuse stale destination. Notes document or insertion anchor changes: refuse rather than mutate the wrong note. Agent Chat thread/generation changes: honor frozen policy; never silently target another thread. Replayed delivery ID: no second insertion; receipt reports duplicate. Mutation outcome unknown: do not advertise an unsafe same-destination retry. History save fails: no unconditional “Your transcript is safe” claim unless another owning layer proves preservation. Recovery callback missing: enabled recovery actions must not be rendered. Recording → confirming → recording via Escape: no dropped capture and no duplicate submit callback. Confirming with empty transcript: Enter is swallowed and does not submit. Processing overlay hidden and reopened: phase, transcript, target, and progress remain coherent. Close then reopen during the locked exit tail: no invisible live window, stale exit commit, duplicate registry row, or lost focus. Microphone popup ArrowUp/ArrowDown: rendered selection and getElements selection move together. Popup device-list reorder during the same generation: old semantic IDs cannot select a different physical device. Stale popup generation close: cannot remove a newer popup or leave an orphan. Failed Dictation automation projection: stable failed status, no raw failure Debug structure. Multi-line caption growth: native frame, GPUI bounds, automation bounds, and layout receipt agree. Reduced motion: static caption/dot values; no temporal animation claim from a screenshot. Global Escape/Enter while an external app is frontmost: actual AppKit event boundary, not only atomic helper tests. Footer actions and local keyboard paths perform the same phase transition. Seeded Dictation findings to confirm BUG-DICT-001 — failed phase projected with raw Debug DictationSessionPhase has a dedicated stable as_automation_str, but the bundled automation collector formats the whole phase with Debug. Since Failed contains DictationFailureState, the automation element can expose internal IDs, destination data, recovery capability structure, and failure internals instead of the closed token failed. Several Dictation logs also use ?phase. Confirm: Bashgit diff -U40 main...HEAD -- \ src/dictation/types.rs \ src/dictation/window.rs \ src/windows/automation_surface_collector.rs | rg -n -C 10 'as_automation_str|format!\("\{:\?\}", state\.phase\)|phase = \?' rg -n \ 'format!\("\{:\?\}", state\.phase\)|phase = \?self\.state\.phase|from_phase = \?previous_phase|to_phase = \?state\.phase' \ src/dictation src/windows Future remediation: Diff--- a/src/windows/automation_surface_collector.rs +++ b/src/windows/automation_surface_collector.rs @@ fn collect_dictation_snapshot(...) - let phase = format!("{:?}", state.phase); + let phase = state.phase.as_automation_str().to_string(); let mut signal = element( "panel:dictation-signal-band", ElementType::Panel, - Some(phase), + Some(phase.clone()), ... ); signal.kind = Some("signal".to_string()); + signal.status_kind = Some(phase.clone()); For logs: Diff- phase = ?self.state.phase, + phase = self.state.phase.as_automation_str(), When failed details are operationally needed, log only the typed failure code and diagnostic fingerprint. Future proof: Construct a Failed state containing private canaries in destination_label, transcript_id, history_entry_id, and diagnostic details. Serialize or inspect the automation snapshot and captured trace. Only "failed", the safe visible headline, typed code, and diagnostic fingerprint may appear. BUG-DICT-002 — keyboard selection does not republish microphone semantics The popup’s select_row changes selected_row_id and notifies the renderer. The automation collector consumes a cached snapshot that is updated during popup creation/sync, not visibly during keyboard selection. Confirm: Bashgit diff -U40 main...HEAD -- \ src/dictation/microphone_popup_window.rs \ src/windows/automation_surface_collector.rs | rg -n -C 12 'fn select_row|selected_row_id|upsert_dictation_microphone' rg -n \ 'fn select_row|upsert_dictation_microphone_prompt_popup_snapshot' \ src/dictation/microphone_popup_window.rs \ src/windows/automation_surface_collector.rs Future remediation: Diff--- a/src/dictation/microphone_popup_window.rs +++ b/src/dictation/microphone_popup_window.rs @@ fn select_row(&mut self, row_index: usize, cx: &mut Context<Self>) { let Some(row) = self.snapshot.rows.get(row_index) else { return; }; self.snapshot.selected_row_id = Some(row.row_id.clone()); + if InlinePopupLifecycle::snapshot(&self.lifecycle).1 == InlinePopupPhase::Open { + crate::windows::automation_surface_collector:: + upsert_dictation_microphone_prompt_popup_snapshot( + DICTATION_MICROPHONE_POPUP_AUTOMATION_ID, + self.generation.get(), + &self.snapshot, + ); + } cx.notify(); } Future runtime proof: Open popup; capture getElements; press ArrowDown through the real window; capture getElements again. Exactly one row changes selected=true and both focused_semantic_id and selected_semantic_id name that row. BUG-DICT-003 — overlay growth can leave stale automation bounds The bundled native resize path calls AppKit setFrame, while automation bounds are registered on initial open. No corresponding bounds update is visible in set_state. Confirm: Bashrg -n \ 'resize_overlay_height|set_automation_bounds|dictation_automation_bounds|OVERLAY_MAX_EXTRA_CAPTION_LINES' \ src/dictation/window.rs src/windows Future remediation: Diff--- a/src/dictation/window.rs +++ b/src/dictation/window.rs @@ -fn resize_overlay_height(window: &mut Window, target_height: f32) { +fn resize_overlay_height( + window: &mut Window, + target_height: f32, +) -> Option<gpui::Bounds<gpui::Pixels>> { ... let new_frame = ... let () = msg_send![ns_window, setFrame: new_frame display: YES]; + Some(convert_native_frame_to_gpui_bounds(new_frame, window)) } @@ fn set_state(...) - resize_overlay_height(window, target_height); + if let Some(bounds) = resize_overlay_height(window, target_height) { + crate::windows::set_automation_bounds( + DICTATION_OVERLAY_AUTOMATION_ID, + Some(dictation_automation_bounds(bounds)), + ); + } The actual implementation must use the repository’s existing coordinate-conversion owner rather than inventing a second conversion formula. Runtime proof: Open at 100px; feed enough transcript for at least three extra lines; compare CGWindow/native frame, window.bounds(), listWindows bounds, and automation_layout_info.window_height. All four agree within the existing rounding tolerance. BUG-DICT-004 — waveform layout receipt uses a fixed 48-point width The rendered waveform width is: 9 bars × 3 points + 8 gaps × 3 points = 51 points The bundled automation_layout_info reports 48. Future remediation: Diff+const WAVEFORM_TOTAL_WIDTH_PX: f32 = + WAVEFORM_BAR_COUNT as f32 * WAVEFORM_BAR_WIDTH_PX + + (WAVEFORM_BAR_COUNT.saturating_sub(1)) as f32 * WAVEFORM_BAR_GAP_PX; @@ fn automation_layout_info(...) - (width - 48.0) / 2.0, + (width - WAVEFORM_TOTAL_WIDTH_PX) / 2.0, ... - 48.0, + WAVEFORM_TOTAL_WIDTH_PX, Classify as a receipt defect, not a visible rendering defect, unless runtime bounds show otherwise. Mandatory Dictation proof gaps GAP-DICT-005 — “transcript is safe” must be owning-layer proof Trace every DictationFailureState construction: Bashrg -n 'DictationFailureState \{|history_saved:|preservation_receipt:' \ src/dictation tests The statement is verified only when all failure paths establish one of: history write succeeded durably, or immutable transcript remains owned by a reachable recovery state. A struct field or optimistic message is not enough. GAP-DICT-006 — target identity Debug redaction Trace logging of: DictationTargetSelection FrozenDictationDestination DictationDeliveryRequest DictationFailureState DictationSessionPhase Bashrg -n \ '\?[a-zA-Z_]*(selection|destination|request|failure|phase)|Debug for Dictation' \ src/dictation src/windows Derived Debug containing display labels, document IDs, thread IDs, or window identities must not be treated as privacy-safe merely because transcript text has a custom redacted Debug. Batch 4 — Notes audit Complete path grouping Canonical search, data, and actions src/notes/actions_panel.rs src/notes/ai_scope.rs src/notes/day_switcher.rs src/notes/mod.rs src/notes/search_model.rs src/notes/storage.rs Audit: one search corpus and rank across regular notes and day notes, stable IDs and destination verbs, loading/failure/prior-snapshot semantics, storage failures and atomic mutations, scope boundaries for whole note, selection, current line, resource, and attached note, no synchronous UI-thread claim without call-site proof. Notes window shell and lifecycle src/notes/window.rs src/notes/window/contract.rs src/notes/window/focus.rs src/notes/window/init.rs src/notes/window/layout.rs src/notes/window/window_ops.rs Audit: singleton/instance generation, open, close, focus, hide, reactivation, and stale handles, exact autosize geometry and footer accounting, native versus GPUI bounds, locked Notes entry/body reveal semantics without retuning. Input, navigation, and mutation src/notes/window/clipboard_ops.rs src/notes/window/keyboard.rs src/notes/window/navigation.rs src/notes/window/notes.rs src/notes/window/notes_actions.rs Audit: one owner per advertised shortcut, Cmd+Enter handoff, Cmd+P search, Escape/Cmd+W behavior, selection-safe clipboard operations, note/day navigation and dirty-content handling. Panels and rendering src/notes/window/panels.rs src/notes/window/render_editor_body.rs src/notes/window/render_editor_titlebar.rs src/notes/window/render_ui.rs Audit: shared component/token use, active panel and focus correspondence, actions/search panel element collection, titlebar actions and disabled reasons, no one-off glass or motion values. Handoff and tests src/notes/window/ai_handoff.rs src/notes/window/tests.rs Exact handoff anchors: compose_note_ai_target build_notes_ai_handoff_payload handoff_selected_note_to_main_agent_chat dispatch_notes_ai_handoff_to_main schedule_ai_handoff_retry consume_staged_cart_rows finish_successful_ai_handoff record_ai_handoff_receipt restore_notes_host_return notes_host_return_decision Call-site map: Bashrg -n \ 'handoff_selected_note_to_main_agent_chat|schedule_ai_handoff_retry|dispatch_notes_ai_handoff_to_main|consume_staged_cart_rows|record_ai_handoff_receipt|restore_notes_host_return|resolve_notes_autosize|load_note_search_state|rank_note_search_rows|current_focus_surface|focus_transition_generation' \ src/notes src/windows tests scripts Required Notes scenarios Saved note handoff uses unsaved live editor content, not stale disk content. Unsaved nonempty draft stages successfully with an instance-scoped identity. Empty draft/no note fails closed and leaves both windows unchanged. Notes remains open when main Agent Chat opens. Cold main-window open taking longer than 50ms does not lose the user action. Repeated handoff while main is starting does not duplicate primary context or cart attachments. Request-ID mismatch consumes no cart items. Primary failure consumes no cart items. Accepted and canonical duplicate supplements consume only their matching cart rows. Missing, forged, or mismatched supplement outcomes consume nothing. Partial storage deletion is surfaced honestly. The receipt’s accepted/duplicate/failed/missing totals agree with status and actual cart rows. Main window or hook unavailable after the bounded retry records a typed failure, not a false staged receipt. Return after Notes instance/window/focus replacement is refused. Determine whether return means only “reactivate current Notes focus” or “restore exact document/selection/scroll.” Align claims with implementation. Cmd+P combines notes and day notes with stable selection through refresh. Failed refresh retains prior rows without claiming fresh results. Day file disappears between search and open: typed failure, no stale content. Unicode title/query: ranking tiers remain correct for multibyte text. Search/actions panel open: rendered focus and automation focus agree. Long soft-wrapped note: measured display lines drive autosize; no footer overlap. Native footer host is either already excluded from content bounds or explicitly included—never double-counted or omitted. Copy/paste at multibyte selection boundaries does not panic or split UTF-8. Closing/reopening Notes cannot let a stale return snapshot focus the new instance. Seeded Notes findings to confirm BUG-NOTES-001 — one fixed 50ms handoff retry is not a readiness protocol The bundle shows a single 50ms timer after requesting the main window. This is a plausible regression when a cold main window or Agent Chat host takes longer than 50ms to become dispatch-ready. Confirm exact call order and registration timing: Bashgit diff -U50 main...HEAD -- src/notes/window/ai_handoff.rs | rg -n -C 15 'schedule_ai_handoff_retry|from_millis\(50\)|MainWindowUnavailable' rg -n \ 'register_notes_ai_main_handoff_hook|get_main_window_handle|request_show_main_window|schedule_ai_handoff_retry' \ src Classify as Regression-Candidate/Temporal until a delayed-readiness boundary test fails. Future remediation: Diff--- a/src/notes/window/ai_handoff.rs +++ b/src/notes/window/ai_handoff.rs @@ +const NOTES_HANDOFF_READY_DEADLINE: Duration = Duration::from_millis(750); +const NOTES_HANDOFF_RETRY_INTERVAL: Duration = Duration::from_millis(25); fn schedule_ai_handoff_retry( &mut self, payload: NotesAiHandoffPayload, cx: &mut Context<Self>, ) { let this = cx.entity().downgrade(); cx.spawn(async move |_this, cx| { - cx.background_executor() - .timer(Duration::from_millis(50)) - .await; - ... + let deadline = Instant::now() + NOTES_HANDOFF_READY_DEADLINE; + loop { + cx.background_executor() + .timer(NOTES_HANDOFF_RETRY_INTERVAL) + .await; + + let outcome = cx.update(|cx| { + let Some(entity) = this.upgrade() else { + return RetryDisposition::OwnerGone; + }; + entity.update(cx, |app, cx| { + app.try_same_materialized_handoff_payload(&payload, cx) + }) + }); + + match outcome { + RetryDisposition::Complete => break, + RetryDisposition::StillStarting if Instant::now() < deadline => continue, + RetryDisposition::StillStarting + | RetryDisposition::PermanentFailure + | RetryDisposition::OwnerGone => { + record_one_terminal_failure(...); + break; + } + } + } }).detach(); } Prefer an existing main-host-ready signal over polling when one already exists. Do not introduce a second window-readiness framework. Future proof: Delay main Agent Chat readiness until attempt three. Assert one user action, one request_id, one primary stage, one stage per supplement, and one terminal receipt. Repeat with readiness beyond the deadline and assert one typed failure. BUG-NOTES-002 — supplement accounting can disagree with status The bundled status calculation counts missing outcomes as failures, but record_ai_handoff_receipt counts only explicit Failed outcomes. In addition, delete_note_cart_items returns a count that is not visibly compared with the requested consumable count. Confirm storage semantics: Bashgit diff -U60 main...HEAD -- \ src/notes/window/ai_handoff.rs \ src/notes/storage.rs | rg -n -C 15 'consume_staged_cart_rows|reported_ids|supplemental_failed_count|delete_note_cart_items' Future remediation: Diff+struct NotesSupplementAccounting { + consumable_ids: Vec<String>, + accepted: usize, + duplicate: usize, + explicit_failed: usize, + missing: usize, + unrecognized: usize, +} +fn account_supplements( + attachments: &[NotesHandoffAttachment], + outcome: &NotesAiMainHandoffOutcome, +) -> NotesSupplementAccounting { + // One canonical computation shared by cart consumption, status, + // receipt fields, and logs. +} @@ fn consume_staged_cart_rows(...) - let consumable_ids = consumable_cart_item_ids(...); - let explicit_failed_count = ... - let failed_count = ... + let accounting = account_supplements(...); @@ - Ok(consumed) => (status, consumed), + Ok(consumed) if consumed == accounting.consumable_ids.len() => (status, consumed), + Ok(consumed) => { + tracing::warn!( + event = "notes_ai_handoff_cart_partial_consume", + expected_count = accounting.consumable_ids.len(), + consumed_count = consumed, + ); + (NotesAiHandoffStatus::StagedCartRetained, consumed) + } @@ fn record_ai_handoff_receipt(...) - supplemental_failed_count = explicit failed count + supplemental_failed_count = + accounting.explicit_failed + accounting.missing + accounting.unrecognized Future test: accepted, duplicate, explicit failure, missing outcome, forged key, and partial delete count all produce mutually consistent status, receipt, and remaining cart rows. GAP-NOTES-003 — “return snapshot” currently appears broader than restoration NotesHostReturnSnapshot captures document identity, content generation, selection, scroll, mode, aliases, search state, and focus. The bundled restore_notes_host_return validates instance/window/focus generation and then restores only the focus surface. Resolve the product contract: If return means “bring the still-current Notes window forward,” rename and reduce the snapshot to what is actually restored. If return means “return to the exact note and editing position,” validate document generation and restore document, selection, scroll, mode, and panel state only when safe. Do not describe exact restoration in the article until a real boundary test proves it. BUG-NOTES-004 — automation may report editor focus while another Notes panel owns focus The bundled collect_notes_snapshot always sets focused_semantic_id to input:notes-editor and labels the projection Full, while Notes now has browse, actions, preview, and dialog focus surfaces. Confirm with: Bashrg -n \ 'collect_notes_snapshot|focused_semantic_id|current_focus_surface|NotesFocusSurface|get_notes_.*snapshot|get_notes_editor_text' \ src/notes src/windows/automation_surface_collector.rs Future remediation architecture: Diff--- a/src/notes/window/contract.rs +++ b/src/notes/window/contract.rs +pub(crate) struct NotesAutomationSnapshot { + pub mode: NotesViewMode, + pub focus_surface: NotesFocusSurface, + pub editor: Option<NotesEditorAutomationSnapshot>, + pub titlebar_actions: Vec<NotesActionDescriptor>, + pub panel_elements: Vec<ElementInfo>, + pub document_identity: Option<SemanticChipSpec>, +} --- a/src/notes/mod.rs +++ b/src/notes/mod.rs +pub(crate) fn get_notes_automation_snapshot( + cx: &gpui::App, +) -> Option<NotesAutomationSnapshot> { ... } --- a/src/windows/automation_surface_collector.rs +++ b/src/windows/automation_surface_collector.rs - collect independent editor/titlebar getters and assume editor focus + consume one NotesAutomationSnapshot built from the same state used by render + derive focused_semantic_id from focus_surface + use Partial quality only when the owning snapshot is unavailable Future runtime proof: open editor, Cmd+P browse panel, actions panel, preview, and dialog; getElements must name the rendered focus owner in every state. Batch 5 — Platform, focus, resize, and automation registry audit Exact paths src/main_window_preflight/build.rs src/platform/gpui_event_simulator.rs src/platform/visibility_focus.rs src/window_resize/arg_layout.rs src/window_resize/mod.rs src/windows/automation_registry.rs src/windows/automation_runtime_handles.rs src/windows/automation_surface_collector.rs src/windows/automation_transaction_provider.rs src/windows/mod.rs Required invariants Every visible registered automation window has a valid runtime handle unless explicitly panel-only. Every generated popup registration and handle use the same generation. A stale close/remove call cannot remove a newer generation. Registry focused and visible values agree with