shot request set Write these into 06-screenshot-requests.md. Capture only those the manager explicitly assigns. SHOT-04-01 — Flow active and archived conversation State: one active thread with two turns; one archived thread selected in history; read-only state visible. Required: thread/history affordance, retained-turn copy, selected archive identity, no raw path. Type: static. Can prove: information architecture and visible read-only distinction. Cannot prove: persistence, tombstones, collision resistance, restart behavior. Caption: “Flow conversations now present durable active and archived threads, but their storage identity still needs collision-resistant proof.” SHOT-04-02 — Unified Notes search State: Cmd+P with one ordinary note, one day note, one pinned note, and a nonempty query. Required: shared row language, title, preview metadata, destination verb, stable selection. Type: static. Caption: “Notes and day pages now share one search language, reducing surface drift across the editor and launcher.” SHOT-04-03 — Notes handoff with both windows visible State: live unsaved edit in Notes; main Agent Chat opened with explicit note context; Notes remains open. Required: Notes content area, Agent Chat context chip, no private content in article capture. Type: static plus separate temporal receipt. Caption: “The handoff keeps Notes as the source of truth while staging a live snapshot in the main Agent Chat.” SHOT-04-04 — Armed Dictation recording anatomy State: recording, synthetic transcript present, target set, reduced-motion capture preferred. Required: timer, Paste/Today/Ask/Send quick chips, target badge, caption, footer actions. Type: static. Caption: “Dictation consolidates destination choice, live transcript, and the next safe action in one compact overlay.” SHOT-04-05 — Microphone popup after keyboard movement State: popup open; keyboard selection moved from System Default to a second fixture device. Required: visible selected row; pair with a redacted get