ression”Unverified-ClaimComment, test name, receipt, or prior ledger asserts behavior without adequate proof.“Unverified”BlockedScope drift, unavailable harness, environmental interference, or build failure prevents classification.State the blocker only Severity and confidence are separate. A high-severity issue may remain a candidate; a low-severity geometry receipt may be statically verified. Article-ready integration hunk The worker records this verbatim in 07-article-ready.md. Replace bracketed evidence IDs only with confirmed lane IDs; do not strengthen the prose. Markdown## Windows, Flow, Notes, and Dictation: coherence outran proof Across 45 changed files, the branch moves several interaction-heavy surfaces toward typed state, shared descriptors, explicit generations, and richer automation projections. Flow gains threaded conversation persistence; Notes shares search and stages live editor context into the main Agent Chat; Dictation freezes destinations, preserves transcripts for recovery, and uses one compact overlay across recording, processing, delivery, and failure. These are substantial structural improvements, but structure is not the same as runtime trust. The highest-risk boundaries are the ones a screenshot cannot settle: conversation storage identity, cold-window handoff readiness, keyboard focus, generation-safe popup teardown, native resize synchronization, delivery idempotency, and close/reopen races during the locked glass exit tail. The audit therefore separates behavior-tested rules from native lifecycle proof and labels every remaining assertion explicitly. **Confidence:** Plausible improvement, with confirmed exceptions and proof gaps listed below. **Evidence:** `.notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/04-window-flows/10-worker-report.md` ### Confirmed improvements - [Insert only `IMP-*` findings promoted to Verified-Behavior or Verified-Runtime.] ### Confirmed or likely regressions - [Insert `BUG-*` findings with exact state → wrong result and confidence.] ### Proof gaps - [Insert material `GAP-*` findings; do not restate every skipped test.] > Screenshot: **A popup is trustworthy only when its visible selection and > automation selection move together.** Shared ledger integration hunk Record this in 09-integration-hunks.md; the manager applies it to the shared ledger. Markdown| Lane | Scope | Accounting | Strongest verified improvement | Highest risk | Confidence | Evidence | |---|---:|---|---|---|---|---| | 04-window-flows | 45 paths | 45/45 reviewed; +10,470/-2,302 reconciled | `<IMP-ID>: <one sentence>` | `<BUG/GAP-ID>: <one sentence>` | `<label>` | `.notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/04-window-flows/10-worker-report.md` | No row may say 45/45 until every 01-path-review.tsv row is complete. Next-step cards for the Paper Fold article These are the package’s contribution to the article’s largest substantive section. Write confirmed cards as JSONL and preserve unsupported ones as proof gaps. WF-01 — Make Flow transcript identity collision-resistant Priority: P0 if BUG-FLOW-001 is branch-introduced. Targets: src/flows/session.rs::conversation_file_name, load_persisted_conversation_from. Change: add an original-identity hash to the filename; migrate old files only after embedded-path validation. Proof: two deliberately colliding paths persist and reload independently; legacy adoption cannot cross paths. Do not do: truncate or sanitize more aggressively as a substitute for hashing. WF-02 — Publish closed, redacted Dictation phase semantics Priority: P0. Targets: DictationSessionPhase::as_automation_str, collect_dictation_snapshot, phase trace fields. Change: stable phase token in automation; typed code/fingerprint in diagnostics; no Debug projection of failed state. Proof: private canaries absent from getElements and logs. Do not do: hide useful safe recovery copy or weaken automation coverage. WF-03 — Keep popup semantics synchronized with keyboard state Priority: P1. Targets: DictationMicrophonePopupWindow::select_row, popup cache publisher. Change: republish the generation-scoped snapshot after selection changes; derive stable row identity from a redacted device identity rather than index when refresh can reorder rows. Proof: Arrow navigation changes render and automation atomically; stale semantic IDs cannot select another device. WF-04 — Replace Notes’ fixed sleep with bounded readiness Priority: P1. Targets: schedule_ai_handoff_retry, main host readiness owner. Change: reuse an existing ready signal or bounded deadline loop while preserving one materialized payload and request ID. Proof: delayed host becomes ready after multiple intervals; stage occurs once. Deadline expiry produces one failure receipt. WF-05 — Make Notes automation come from the owning view state Priority: P1. Targets: src/notes/window/contract.rs, src/notes/mod.rs, collect_notes_snapshot. Change: one owning snapshot for mode, focus, panel elements, editor, actions, and document identity. Proof: editor, search, actions, preview, and dialog states each project their actual focus owner. Do not do: add a second Notes state machine inside the collector. WF-06 — Synchronize native resize and automation geometry Priority: P1. Targets: resize_overlay_height, Dictation registry bounds, automation_layout_info. Change: publish the resulting native frame through the existing coordinate owner; derive repeated geometry from shared constants. Proof: native, GPUI, registry, and layout receipts agree after multiline growth. WF-07 — Unify Notes supplement accounting Priority: P2. Targets: consume_staged_cart_rows, record_ai_handoff_receipt, delete_note_cart_items. Change: one accounting result drives consumption, status, receipt, and logs. Proof: accepted, duplicate, failed, missing, forged, and partially deleted outcomes remain consistent. WF-08 — Prove focus and visibility as transactions Priority: P1. Targets: visibility_focus.rs, automation transaction provider, registry/runtime handles. Change: only